    "hints": {
      "adam.bypass_open": "The service path is open. We can build from here. You can return through an opened door even when the supply changes.",
      "adam.bypass_power": "That relay feed holds. The service door can open now. This path is one you built.",
      "adam.danger": "Watch the arc. Step back toward the west path and isolate the supply before working on it.",
      "adam.isolated": "The damaged feed is isolated. We can repair the main supply or build a relay at the bypass socket. You choose the connection.",
      "adam.live_fault": "I'm here. This nook has reserve light, but we are still inside Jenison. Start with what still responds. Follow the west signal path to the supply, or look around before we go.",
      "adam.pencil": "The page can stay blank. You can rest, return to what you built or look toward the distant RTX core. I'll follow your lead.",
      "adam.repaired_connected": "That connection holds. Main power is back. Open the main entrance when you're ready, and watch the warm circuits answer.",
      "adam.repaired_isolated": "Your repair holds. Reconnect the main feed at the isolation switch when you're ready; the bypass remains another option.",
      "adam.shelter": "We reached shelter. This is different from the little reserve nook. There is a workbench, a quiet place to pause and the Pencil Room ahead. The lamp is yours to help with or leave for now.",
      "inspect.042bef85-8583-4ca3-982d-2186b87cf01a.action": "read",
      "inspect.042bef85-8583-4ca3-982d-2186b87cf01a.source": "Echos Within, XML paragraph 69, Never Felt More Pain. The red toy-truck memory is sourced; this keepsake and future vehicle connection are game adaptations.",
      "inspect.042bef85-8583-4ca3-982d-2186b87cf01a.text": "Your writing keeps a happy fragment of Adam pushing you in a red electric toy truck. This little keepsake holds that fragment without asking you to revisit the painful events around it. Later, building vehicles can grow from this memory; here, you can simply look and continue when you want.",
      "inspect.320d52c5-8a5c-4f7d-b86b-e6a2640b1bb1.action": "seat",
      "inspect.320d52c5-8a5c-4f7d-b86b-e6a2640b1bb1.source": "Echos Within, XML paragraphs 270 and 1165: reflective imagining. Two seats and this optional quiet panel are authored adaptations. No historical dialogue is asserted.",
      "inspect.320d52c5-8a5c-4f7d-b86b-e6a2640b1bb1.text": "Your reflective writing imagines Adam nearby. These two seats give that feeling a place inside the shelter. You may take a quiet reading pause here, ask Adam to wait, or carry on together. This is an imagined space made from your writing, not a claim that a conversation happened here. No response or emotional choice is required.",
      "inspect.979c61b9-43e7-4e99-95f4-3ebcbc082e36.action": "read",
      "inspect.979c61b9-43e7-4e99-95f4-3ebcbc082e36.source": "Echos Within, XML paragraphs 946-947, inform protection and making room. The Caretaker and lamp quest are fictional gameplay; no family member is represented by this NPC.",
      "inspect.979c61b9-43e7-4e99-95f4-3ebcbc082e36.text": "Shelter becomes meaningful when there is room for someone else. The Caretaker's lamp is an optional task: offer help or decline through the existing choice controls. You can still reach the Pencil Room either way. This fictional character is here to give you a small, practical choice about the space you have restored.",
      "inspect.9aafc2d9-700c-4602-a5fd-809048459216.action": "read",
      "inspect.9aafc2d9-700c-4602-a5fd-809048459216.source": "Echos Within, XML paragraph 332, Adam My Brother Always. Pencil Room is a game adaptation named in the project, not a literal location in the memoir.",
      "inspect.9aafc2d9-700c-4602-a5fd-809048459216.text": "In your writing, a pencil preserves memories of Adam and your cousin, carrying a value possessions cannot replace. This page stays blank. There is no invented final letter to discover and no answer you must write. You have reached a place you can return to, with Adam's memory beside you and a larger world still waiting to be built.",
      "inspect.aa5b0367-f4ee-4f3c-a254-b676c1e414ba.action": "read",
      "inspect.aa5b0367-f4ee-4f3c-a254-b676c1e414ba.source": "Authored engine instructions for the existing Build, repair, connect-bypass and door-latch mechanics. The restoration theme is informed by Echos Within, XML paragraph 1145.",
      "inspect.aa5b0367-f4ee-4f3c-a254-b676c1e414ba.text": "A spare part can become a new path. Keep the damaged supply isolated. Aim down at the marked socket near the service entrance and use Build to create a relay; repair it if needed, then interact with the healthy relay to connect the bypass. You can dismantle and rebuild it. A door already opened stays a usable return route when power changes.",
      "inspect.be12f535-4053-48ae-a623-5cab920fc31f.action": "read",
      "inspect.be12f535-4053-48ae-a623-5cab920fc31f.source": "Echos Within, XML paragraph 682, Always Family Guy. Controller placement and gameplay guidance are authored adaptations, not a quotation from Adam.",
      "inspect.be12f535-4053-48ae-a623-5cab920fc31f.text": "You wrote that Adam taught you to look and turn in games. Start by looking around this little reserve-lit corner. The motherboard is the world you will build, one connection at a time. Adam's memory can Follow, Wait or Recall; choosing your own pace remains yours.",
      "inspect.faadd037-d9cc-412a-b261-e84c85dc8401.action": "read",
      "inspect.faadd037-d9cc-412a-b261-e84c85dc8401.source": "Mechanical design adaptation. Echos Within, XML paragraph 1145, informs making something useful from damage; this electrical diagnostic is not a memoir event.",
      "inspect.faadd037-d9cc-412a-b261-e84c85dc8401.text": "The fault station has two honest ways forward. Inspect the damaged supply, isolate it at the nearby switch, then either repair the main supply and reconnect it or build a relay at the bypass socket. Watch the current state and Adam's guidance. Neither route proves more about you; each changes how this opening records your first connection."
    },
